als": {"margin": -3.02, "lean": -8.0, "environment": 7.9, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -0.92}, "rating_margin": -10.89, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.33, "baseline_margin": -5.26, "analyst_adjustment": 2.26, "key_factors": ["Hendrix College poll shows Jones up 4 in a high-quality LV survey", "Hill holds large financial advantage ($2.97M cash vs $191K)", "Raters mostly call it Likely or Solid R despite the polling", "R+8 district fundamentals favor Republicans"], "rationale": "The district's R+8 lean and Hill's overwhelming money advantage point Republican, but the sole high-quality poll (Hendrix, LV, n=1112) shows Jones leading by 4, and national Democrats are investing attention. That justifies moving several points toward Jones from the fundamentals-based estimate, though markets still price Hill near 80%.", "watch": "Any follow-up polling confirming or refuting the Hendrix result, plus outside spending on either side, would most change the outlook.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent French Hill (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent French Hill seeks another term in Arkansas's 2nd District, a seat with an R+8 partisan lean that he has held since 2017. Democrat Chris Jones, a 2022 gubernatorial nominee, has drawn national attention and surrogates including Buttigieg, Harris, and Kennedy, and a Hendrix College poll from mid-August showed him leading Hill by four points among likely voters.\n\nHill nonetheless holds a decisive financial edge, with nearly $3 million on hand and outside support, while Jones has about $191,000. Most expert raters still place the race at Likely or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Hill roughly an 80% chance. The race is closer than the district's fundamentals suggest, but Hill remains favored.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}]}